      "9": {
        "attributes": {
          "font-size": {
            "type": "number",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "LENGTH\n\nThe Length node gives you the amount of elements in a collection.\nThis is mostly used for strings when you want to know how long the string is, but it also works with integers if you need that.\n\nIn this example we take the length of \"Hey Wire!\" - which is 9.\nWe add 1 because we want to trim away the entire string.\nWe use this value (10) for the amplitude of the unipolar Sine oscillator which makes it run from 0 to 10.\nThis value determines how much of the string gets cut off, giving us an appearing/disappearing act."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
